  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 19,
    "summary": "Job tells of the ills that have befallen him and then testifies, I know that my Redeemer lives—Job prophesies that he will be resurrected and that in his flesh he will see God.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "How long will ye vex my soul, and break me in pieces with words?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "These ten times have ye reproached me: ye are not ashamed that ye make yourselves strange to me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And be it indeed that I have erred, mine error remaineth with myself.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "If indeed ye will magnify yourselves against me, and plead against me my reproach:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Know now that God hath overthrown me, and hath compassed me with his net.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard: I cry aloud, but there is no judgment.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "HEB justice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 73
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath fenced up my way that I cannot pass, and he hath set darkness in my paths.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath stripped me of my glory, and taken the crown from my head.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath destroyed me on every side, and I am gone: and mine hope hath he removed like a tree.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath also kindled his wrath against me, and he counteth me unto him as one of his enemies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "His troops come together, and raise up their way against me, and encamp round about my tabernacle.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "HEB tent."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath put my brethren far from me, and mine acquaintance are verily estranged from me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "My kinsfolk have failed, and my familiar friends have forgotten me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Ps. 31:11 (11–12)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "They that dwell in mine house, and my maids, count me for a stranger: I am an alien in their sight.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "I called my servant, and he gave me no answer; I entreated him with my mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "My breath is strange to my wife, though I entreated for the children’s sake of mine own body.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "OR spirit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, young children despised me; I arose, and they spake against me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "All my inward friends abhorred me: and they whom I loved are turned against me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "OR intimate."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "My bone cleaveth to my skin and to my flesh, and I am escaped with the skin of my teeth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 19:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 19,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Have pity upon me, have pity upon me, O ye my friends; for the hand of God hath touched me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Friendship."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Job 1:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
